Redux Store Explained
What is a Redux Store?
A Redux Store is the central container that holds all the application state in a Redux app. It's a single source of truth for your entire application's data.

Think of it like a database for your frontend — it holds all the data your app needs to work with.

Your Store Setup (src/app/store.ts)

export const store = configureStore({
  reducer: {
    [studentsApiSlice.reducerPath]: studentsApiSlice.reducer,
  },
  middleware: (getDefaultMiddleware) =>
    getDefaultMiddleware().concat(studentsApiSlice.middleware),
})
Here's what's happening:

Concept	Explanation
configureStore	Redux Toolkit function that creates the store (replaces older createStore)
reducer	Functions that determine how state changes in response to actions
middleware	Extends store capabilities (e.g., for async API calls)
Core Store Methods
The store provides 4 main methods:


// 1. Get current state
store.getState() → returns the entire state tree

// 2. Update state (the ONLY way to change state)
store.dispatch(action) → sends an action to update state

// 3. Listen for changes
store.subscribe(listener) → runs a function whenever state changes

// 4. Replace a reducer
store.replaceReducer(nextReducer) → for code-splitting/hot reloading
How State Flows in Redux

Component → dispatch(action) → Store → Reducer → New State → Component re-renders
Component dispatches an action (e.g., "ADD_STUDENT")
Store passes it to the reducer
Reducer returns new state based on the action
Store updates and notifies all subscribers
Components connected to that state re-render
Two Important Derived Types in Your Code

// Used for reading state
export type RootState = ReturnType<typeof store.getState>

// Used for dispatching actions
export type AppDispatch = typeof store.dispatch
These are used in your typed hooks (src/app/hooks.ts):


export const useAppDispatch: () => AppDispatch = useDispatch
export const useAppSelector: TypedUseSelectorHook<RootState> = useSelector
This gives you TypeScript autocompletion and type safety when:

Selecting data from the store → useAppSelector(state => state...)
Dispatching actions → useAppDispatch()
The Provider (src/main.tsx)

<Provider store={store}>
  <App />
</Provider>
The Provider makes the store available to all components in the component tree via React Context. Without it, useSelector and useDispatch wouldn't work.

Summary
Term	Purpose
Store	Holds all application state
Reducer	Pure function: (state, action) => newState
Action	Plain object describing what happened {type: 'ADD', payload: ...}
Dispatch	Sends an action to the store to update state
Provider	React component that makes store available to children
useSelector	Hook to read data from the store
useDispatch	Hook to send actions to the store
The Redux Store follows a strict rule: state is read-only — the only way to change it is by dispatching an action. This makes state changes predictable and traceable.


